    {
     "read": 0,
     "seconds": 100.4,
     "report": "Reading it as a creature, it does **not** read as a believable monkey — or any animal. It reads as an elongated, hunched, neckless blob with vestigial limbs. Defects, worst first:\n\n1. **Neck / throat junction — gaping tear and hollow interior.** This is the dominant failure. Just below the skull, across the front of the throat, the surface is ripped open into a wide jagged horizontal wound; you can see *inside* the head/neck cavity (a row of torn fragments / \"teeth\"-like shards along the inner rim). The skin has clearly detached from the neck joint rather than bending around it. The back of the neck collapses to a thin blade while the front is blown open — there is no continuous cylindrical neck volume at all.\n\n2. **Pelvis / legs — total collapse, no ground contact.** Below the barrel torso the mesh simply tapers off into nothing; there are no thighs, shins, knees, or feet anywhere in frame. The figure hovers well above the perspective grid with empty space under it. So the \"standing on a grid\" claim is false at this pose — the creature floats, and its silhouette has no lower half. Whatever leg joints exist have collapsed inward/hidden rather than reaching the floor.\n\n3. **Head / face — deformed, featureless, wrong muzzle.** The cranium is an oversized smooth bulb; the ears are flat detached discs stuck on high like handles. There are no eyes,"
    }
