     "read": 0,
     "seconds": 101.6,
     "report": "Looking only at the mesh in the viewport, here is what is wrong with this creature, worst first.\n\n**1. Torn head/neck seam (the rip under the skull).** This is the most serious defect and it is not a pose artifact — the skin has actually separated from the joint. There is a horizontal jagged tear running across the underside of the cranium where the jaw meets the neck column, and through that gap you can see dark interior geometry and a row of spike-like protrusions (exposed \"teeth\"/inner faces). The head reads as if it were sliced off the body and tilted forward on a hinge, exactly consistent with the spine_upper flexion shown in the readout. A rotating joint should fold the surface; here it has ripped it open. There is also a second dark pinch/crease just below that tear at the throat, so the whole head-to-neck transition is broken rather than articulated.\n\n**2. Hind limbs collapsed / no ground contact.** Below the narrow torso there is simply nothing — the body terminates in a rounded stump with only a small nub protruding (a vestigial tail or groin blob), and no thighs, shins, knees, or feet are present anywhere on the silhouette. The perspective grid directly beneath the figure is empty: the creature is floating, not standing. Whatever contact should exist between feet and ground is absent, so the pose has no honest weight-bearing foundation.\n\n**3. Proportions and silhouette read as a stretched alien, not a monkey.** The cranium is grossly oversized relative to the trunk; the neck is an absurdly long smooth tube (giraffe-like) that dwarfs the torso; the arms are over-long, thin, and splayed outward with no"
