     "report": "Reading the viewport purely as anatomy, here is what breaks the creature, worst first.\n\n**1. Neck / jaw junction — torn open with spiked interior.** This is the dominant defect. The lower face and upper neck have sheared apart into a dark horizontal cavity; along its lower lip you can see a row of jagged spike fragments (the \"teeth\" are broken geometry, not teeth). The skin above that gap is stretched thin over a protruding brow-shelf, and below it the neck tube flares with frayed triangle edges. It reads as ripped-open flesh at exactly the place a creature's head should meet its throat — torn skin + hole + spikes in one cluster.\n\n**2. Legs and feet — absent / collapsed.** Below the narrow waist there is no leg structure at all: the torso tapers into a single rounded stump that just merges with the grid plane. No thighs, knees, shins, ankles, or feet are visible. So the silhouette has no lower body, and ground contact is dishonest — nothing is actually standing on anything; it's a smooth blob kissing the floor line rather than weight-bearing feet.\n\n**3. Chest — detached patch with an oval hole.** The rounded chest bulge reads as a separate inflated patch sitting *on* the torso (its own highlight, its own silhouette edge) rather than continuous volume, and at its lower border there is a clear dark elliptical opening — a literal hole in the front of the body.\n\n**4. Hands / fingers — clawed spikes.** The digits are thin splayed spikes with no knuckle or palm articulation; they look like broken shards fused to the wrist rather than grasping hands.\n\n**5. Shoulders / upper arms — seam and stretch flaps.** There is a visible cut/crease line across each deltoid where the skin looks peeled back, and the arms themselves are too long and thin for"
