   "reads": [
    {
     "read": 0,
     "seconds": 101.3,
     "report": "Read as an artist, this creature does not hold together. It reads less like a monkey and more like a balloon-headed alien with dangling tendrils. Defects, most severe first:\n\n1. **Head–neck junction (the worst thing on the model).** The head is not attached to the body — it floats above the torso on a stretched neck column, and right where the chin/throat should meet the chest there is a torn, jagged opening. You can see straight into the black interior of the mesh: a horizontal cavity with little vertex \"teeth\" / spikes poking out along the tear line. The skin has been pulled clean off the joint here. This is a hole plus detachment, not just a bad crease.\n\n2. **Pelvis and legs.** There are essentially no legs. Below the ribcage the body collapses inward to a thin pointed nub (a fused stump / tail spike at the crotch) instead of splitting into hips → thighs → shins → feet. Because of that, there is no honest ground contact: the figure tapers to nothing above the grid rather than planting weight on two feet. It looks like it's hovering on tiptoe or floating.\n\n3. **Arms.** Both arms are absurdly long and thin — stick-like, hanging far"
    }
